[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="IslandField" load_steps=2 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/world/SCRIPT_island_field.gd" id="1_field"]

; ROLLED BACK (the user: "roll back the terrain to before the cliffs ... smooth and
; hilly like it used to be"): `mesa_enabled` is off and the cones, springs, rivers
; and trails are back. The settings below are kept for the day they are wanted.
; Steep faces are rock with strata by their angle (the terrain's shader) and the
; cliff models are peppered over them (SCRIPT_cliff_rocks.gd, `pepper`).
;
; TABLELANDS (the user, after v32: "less hills and more like valleys and plateaus
; and like very varied terrain ... a lot of flat plateaus and defined buildable
; areas on those flat plateaus as a global rule"): outside the mere and the crash
; the ground is stepped plateaus, walls, ramps and canyons (`mesa_*`); the two
; cones, the springs and their rivers, and the trails are gone.
;
; ISLAND 003 R2'S FIELD: THE FOGGY FOREST WITH DARK WATER (SCENE_island_003_r2.tscn,
; docs/DOC_island_003_r2.md). The user: "can you make an Island 003 R2, with
; water features? make the water dark, forboding, maybe dark green tinted,
; different from the tropical water", then "no golf, no ruins, no obelisk --- make
; me an island 003 R2 without any of that". Island 003's field
; (ISLANDFIELD_forest_003.tres), the same seed, coast, hills, forest and trails,
; changed only here:
;   * NO GOLF: `golf_min_radius` past any island's size, so the one-hole course is
;     never laid. The safe zone at the middle still is: it is the islet the mere
;     lies round.
;   * NO RUINS: `ruin_enabled` off, so no ring of entrances and nothing under it.
;   * NO OBELISK: `safe_pad_radius` 0, so no pad is levelled for one (and the scene
;     has no Obelisk node).
;   * WATER, by island 006's construction (`FlowTerrain`, docs/DOC_island_006_
;     tropical.md): two low wooded hills and eight springs sending out rivers and
;     creeks on splines, carved to beds under a water surface (`flow_river_spline`,
;     `flow_water_mesh`), running to the coast and over it as falls, or ending in
;     pools; and THE MERE, a ring of still water round the middle's islet
;     (`flow_lagoon_*`), wider and deeper than the tropics' lagoon, its beaches
;     narrow. The hills are lower and fewer than 006's, the springs more: this is
;     a wet wood, not a volcanic island. What makes the water dark is the
;     materials', not the field's (MAT_river_water_003_r2.tres).

